      "message": "Yeah, in order to use a SkDrawable which wraps the FT_Face and not create a picture, all of the code here would need to be in the SkDrawable (the mutex, setting up the state on the FT_Face including loading the glyph slot, etc).\n\nNow that Skia requires FreeType 2.8.1 or newer, I think we can re-write a lot of this locking so we only lock the FT_Face and don\u0027t need a global lock anymore for this. Not sure if that would actually help much in contention since we\u0027re often drawing out of one face, but it\u0027s a step in the right direction.",
